 listen:'Listen for how uncertainty, feedback, change and delivery cadence affect the approach. All approaches still involve planning and responsible decisions.',
 concepts:[['Predictive','Useful when substantial scope and delivery details can be established early. Changes are evaluated using the chosen governance. Prediction does not remove the need to learn.'],['Adaptive','Work evolves through feedback and learning when needs or solutions are uncertain. Planning continues, often at different levels and shorter horizons.'],['Hybrid, iterative and incremental','Hybrid combines approaches to fit the work. Iterative work refines a solution through cycles. Incremental work adds usable pieces. A team can do both.']],
 visual:{type:'compare',title:'ONE CAMPUS · DIFFERENT UNCERTAINTY',nodes:[['Hardware rollout','Plan stable requirements, procurement and controlled installation windows.'],['Visitor experience','Try a small workflow, gather feedback and refine before broader adoption.']],caption:'Together these may form a hybrid approach. Hybrid is deliberate tailoring, not a requirement to split work 50/50.'},
 trap:'“Agile means no plan” and “predictive means no change” are both misleading. Context and feedback matter in every approach.',
 recall:'Explain an iterative improvement and an incremental delivery in this project. Then justify why one component might use a different approach.',
 rubric:['I described refinement as iterative.','I described a usable addition as incremental.','I justified the delivery choice through uncertainty or constraints.'],
 language:'“The physical rollout is predictable, but the workflow needs feedback. We can tailor different delivery approaches while keeping their dependencies visible.”',
 pre:mc('a-pre','Knowledge','A team repeatedly refines the same prototype after user feedback. Which term best describes this?',['Incremental only','Iterative','Operations only'],1,'Iteration refines a solution through repeated cycles.',['A refinement is not necessarily a new usable increment.','','A prototype effort can remain bounded project work.']),
 recallQ:term('a-term','What approach combines predictive and adaptive practices to suit the work?',['hybrid','hybrid approach'],'Hybrid should be tailored deliberately around the work, not selected as a slogan.'),
 lab:map('a-lab','category','Classify the delivery choice.',['Plan a stable hardware rollout with formal change decisions','Learn the workflow through short feedback cycles','Combine a planned hardware release with adaptive workflow design'],['Predictive','Adaptive','Hybrid'],[0,1,2],'The choices reflect different uncertainty and feedback needs, not a ranking from bad to good.'),
 decision:mc('a-decision','Judgment','Users cannot yet agree on the visitor workflow, but hardware requirements are stable. Which proposal fits best?',['Force every detail to be fixed immediately','Remove governance from the entire project','Use planned hardware delivery with short workflow experiments and coordinated dependencies'],2,'Tailor the approach to each component while managing their integration.',['Premature detail can hide uncertainty.','Adaptation does not eliminate accountability.',''],'Methodology confusion'),
 exam:[multi('a-e1','Knowledge','Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.',['Adaptive work includes planning','Predictive projects can evaluate changes','Hybrid always means exactly half agile','Work can be both iterative and incremental'],[0,1,3],'These terms describe delivery and learning patterns; none removes the need for judgment.','Methodology confusion'),mc('a-e2','Systems','Each release adds another usable building to the access system. What does this illustrate most directly?',['A new portfolio each time','Incremental delivery','No planning'],1,'Each release adds a usable portion of capability. It might also involve iterative refinement.',['A usable increment is not a portfolio.','','Delivery in increments can be planned.'])]
